Package: brease
Type: Package
Title: Causally Sound Priors for Binary Experiments
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Nicholas", "Irons", role = c("aut"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4599-7744")),
    person("Carlos", "Cinelli", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "cinellic@uw.edu",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6468-2812"))
  )
Description: Implements the BREASE framework for Bayesian analysis of
    randomized controlled trials with binary outcomes. Parameterizes the
    likelihood in terms of baseline risk, efficacy, and adverse side effects,
    with independent Beta priors that induce dependence between treatment
    arms. Provides exact posterior sampling, analytic marginal likelihoods,
    Bayes factors, and sensitivity analysis tools. Methods based on
    Irons and Cinelli (2025) <doi:10.1214/25-BA1506>.
